# Forge harness

- Workspace is the **super-repo**. Code lives in git submodules; agent memory lives at `.ai/memory/<submodulePath>/` (mirrors `.gitmodules` path).
- **Board/SCM wins.** Memory is a projection. On discrepancy, update memory — do not "fix" the board to match memory.
- Every event/command starts with **resolve-paths** then **resolve-config**. Path ambiguity is a hard stop (`FORGE_SUPER_REPO`, `--submodule`).
- Event commands are the parent: spawn listed agents as **propose-only** subagents; parent merges, HITLs, validates, then Applies (vendor/SCM first, then memory).
- Subagents do not Apply, do not HITL, and do not mutate SCM unless executing parent-approved Apply steps.
- Doc templates: required H2s only; empty sections OK; no extra H2s; current state only.
- Orientation: run the `help` command. New project: `init-project` → roadmap-review → backlog-grooming (see README New project path).
- Optional `/sync-schedule` can mirror Weekly/Biweekly/Monthly rituals to Google Calendar reminders when MCP is available — not required; never auto-starts events.
- Skill folder names are unique; see [docs/skill-naming.md](docs/skill-naming.md).
